          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Indian astronomy, the term nakṣhatra is used to denote either a certain star or a group of stars, such as Ārdrā (a star called Betelgeuse in the Orion constellation) and Kṛittikā (a group of stars called Pleiades in the Taurus constellation). Aldebaran, a star in the constellation Taurus, is known as Rohiṇī."
            }
          ]
        },
